# Electric hood and nose reference pass — 2026-10-29

The owner asked to focus on the hood and nose because the new Electric model still differs substantially from the reference. This pass lowers the front shoulder, forms swept bonnet ridges in the surface, rounds the transition into the bumper, and builds a wider recessed lower intake and taller front air curtains. The light strip follows the new front profile and wraps onto the corners. The back and sides remain outside this pass. The fascia is still simpler than the photograph; this is an incremental improvement, not a claim of a finished match.

[Low front-quarter view](evidence/electric-hood-nose-2026-10-29/compatibility/front-quarter-low-clean.png), [front view](evidence/electric-hood-nose-2026-10-29/compatibility/front-clean.png), [side view](evidence/electric-hood-nose-2026-10-29/compatibility/side-clean.png) and [hood view](evidence/electric-hood-nose-2026-10-29/compatibility/bonnet-clean.png) show the final baked model. The mobile-renderer views were captured on desktop as well. The earlier native screenshot is available in `evidence/electric-new-fastback-2026-10-29/compatibility/`.

The updated builder uses `electric_reference_v2`; 225 full/simple prepared meshes, five racing shadows, the Electric Garage template, catalogue/header/Garage/news images and 49 livery pictures were regenerated. Source hashes in the mesh manifest match the current builders and all manifest files exist. The prior asset version remains available.

Focused actual-mesh regression passed 64/64 for both procedural and prepared geometry, covering the hood/fascia join, unoccluded light samples, rays through all three recessed openings and their returns at both detail levels. General Electric integration passed 15/15, racing model checks 23/23, and actual Garage/race integration 58/58. The detailed model has 117,760 triangles; the simplified visible model has 34,376 and its shadow proxies 3,272. Both desktop renderers captured 16 clean/worn views. Desktop App hitches were observed. A first test run had incorrect node-name expectations and was corrected before the passing runs; the first visual candidate exposed a hidden curtain and corner seam that were corrected.

Reload/reimport and owner appearance and device acceptance remain. No phone test, APK, live account/backend write or deployment was performed.
